Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 18:18:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(sim): restore the LGCP simulation path --
 _sample_cells moves to Point_Process_Model and the z->f decode becomes a
 shared base-class method. TWO STACKED DEFECTS, both audit findings, both
 RED-verified: (1) Phase 2b introduced _sample_cells as a Hawkes_Model method
 while its caller _sim_cox lives on Point_Process_Model -- invalid class
 layering; LGCP_Model.simulate() raised AttributeError('LGCP_Model' object has
 no attribute '_sample_cells'). (2) The VAE-latent decode block
 (z_temporal/z_seasonal/z_spatial -> f_t/f_a/f_xy, w -> b_0) was inlined in
 Hawkes_Model.simulate() ONLY, so LGCP_Model.simulate() raised KeyError('f_t')
 on any z-only parameter dict -- the exact shape of mcmc.get_samples() output,
 which carries sample sites, not deterministics; this predates 2b (present at
 the 2a tip) and masked defect (1) in the RED runs. Every prior simulation
 test exercised Hawkes_Model, including its Cox configurations, which is how a
 broken base-class path survived a 49-test suite. Fix: _sample_cells relocated
 byte-identically to Point_Process_Model (base-class code must not depend on
 child-only methods); the decode block extracted as
 Point_Process_Model._decode_field_parameters (pure lift; one copy, per the
 decode_fields commit's own dedup rationale) and called by BOTH simulate()
 methods; LGCP_Model.simulate() additionally gains the final
 points.sjoin(self.A) clip that Hawkes_Model.simulate() has and that
 _sim_cox's docstring promises ('clipped by simulate()'s A-filter') --
 DECLARED BEHAVIOR CHANGE on the LGCP path: pre-fix (modulo the
 AttributeError) out-of-polygon points were returned for non-rectangular
 domains; no test or pin covered the path. New tests/test_lgcp_sim.py:
 runs+reproducible (RED: KeyError f_t; with a pre-decoded f-dict the
 AttributeError layer reproduces verbatim), z-dict == f-dict twin under a
 shared seed (decode is deterministic; RNG stream untouched), polygon clip on
 an L-shaped domain (79 pre-fix notch points would violate it). Verified:
 52/52; fixed-seed cox_hawkes Hawkes simulate byte-identical across the commit
 (3162 events, exact array equality); all four value+gradient pin configs
 bit-identical; ruff clean on bstpp/.

